{"name":"High Hide White","hex":"#eaebe4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:\n Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty.","Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or to an elevated position.","In or at a great value."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high"},{"term":"hide","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (something) in a place where it will be out of sight or harder to discover.","To put oneself in a place where one will be out of sight or harder to find."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin of an animal.","The human skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hide"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hide (skin)","blocks":[{"text":"A hide or skin is an animal skin treated for human use. \nThe word \"hide\" is related to the Dutch word huid and the German word Haut, which mean skin. The industry defines hides as \"skins\" of large animals e.g. cow, buffalo; while skins refer to \"skins\" of smaller animals: goat, sheep, deer, pig, fish, alligator, snake, etc.\nCommon commercial hides include leather from cattle and other livestock animals, buckskin, alligator skin and snake skin. All are used for shoes, clothes, leather bags, belts, or other fashion accessories. Leather is also used in cars, upholstery, interior decorating, horse tack and harnesses. Skins are sometimes still gathered from hunting and processed at a domestic or artisanal level but most leather making is now industrialized and large-scale. Various tannins are used for this purpose. Hides are also used as processed chews for dogs or other pets."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hide_(skin)","wikidata":"Q3291230"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tanned_leather.JPG/500px-Tanned_leather.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tanned_leather.JPG/1280px-Tanned_leather.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tanned_leather.JPG/500px-Tanned_leather.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh tanned leather","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATanned_leather.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Finishgradingleather.jpg/500px-Finishgradingleather.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Fin